    "causal_summary": "mcp-tooling is the single public advisor identity for nine MCP tool bridges: five workflow modes and four read-only design transports, folded into one parent hub. mcp-chrome-devtools routes developer-driven browser debugging through bdg and its Code Mode fallback. mcp-click-up routes ClickUp task management through cupt and the official MCP. mcp-obsidian routes vault and markdown-note management plus Iconic automation through its CLI and MCP lanes. mcp-aside-devtools drives generic agentic browser work. mcp-notion operates Notion through Code Mode and direct API gap fills. mcp-figma drives Figma Desktop, mcp-refero searches real shipped web-product references, mcp-mobbin researches mobile app patterns, and mcp-magicpath looks up components and design systems through a read-only UTCP CLI manual. Figma, Refero, and Mobbin pair with sk-design-md-generator for measured references, while MagicPath theme evidence pairs with sk-design for judgment. The nine Code Mode-backed members share mcp-code-mode as external infrastructure rather than dissolving that substrate into the hub.",
